            <div xml:id="d995">

                <pb facs="1341" n="1331" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg1331"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.4061 Motion Pictures/9–645: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-09-06T13:00:00-04:00">September 6,
                            1945—1 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1403. Hays Organization has informed Dept. that U. S. film companies advised
                    Chinese authorities holding up remittances under pretext new arrangement
                    negotiated by Embassy (15% remittables at official rate 20 to 1) taking effect
                    September 1. Hays understands agreement provided arrangement effective for year
                    1945 beginning January 1. Please telegraph report clarifying situation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
